<title>BRAZIL: Brazil non-ferrous metals - Jnauary statistics.</title>
<headline>Brazil non-ferrous metals - Jnauary statistics.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production, consumption, imports and exports of Brazilian non-ferrous metals in January 1997 compared with January 1996 were as follows, said the</p>
<p>Secretariat of Mines and Metallurgy.</p>
<p>All figures are in tonnes.</p>
<p>    METAL		    PRODUCTION		    CONSUMPTION</p>
<p>			  1997	 1996	    1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	  100,100    100,900	  22,577     33,479</p>
<p> Lead			 0	    0	     n/a	n/a</p>
<p> Copper		14,838     14,172	  23,039	9,968</p>
<p> Tin		    1,624	1,427	     247	  371</p>
<p> Magnesium		n/a	  n/a	     n/a	  n/a</p>
<p> Nickel		 1,418	1,320	     648	1,072</p>
<p> Zinc		  13,322     15,293	  (1,297)     6,121</p>
<p> METAL			EXPORTS			 IMPORTS</p>
<p>			  1997	 1996	    1997	 1996</p>
<p> Aluminium	   87,618     77,814	  13,475	9,752</p>
<p> Lead			 9	   13	   3,096	  651</p>
<p> Copper		 1,788	8,375	  11,430	5,326</p>
<p> Tin		    1,380	1,056		 1	    0</p>
<p> Magnesium		 63	  595	     657	  196</p>
<p> Nickel		   370	  560	     396	  891</p>
<p> Zinc		   2,556     10,133	     127	1,095</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
